1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:04,054
Four friends want one hotel, but their needs conflict.

2
00:00:04,004 --> 00:00:06,669
One needs step-free access.

3
00:00:06,669 --> 00:00:09,144
Another cares about the beach.

4
00:00:09,144 --> 00:00:11,644
Everyone has a different budget.

5
00:00:11,644 --> 00:00:19,820
I can ask an agent to find the fairest option, and it starts by reading the group's real, current workspace through Web M C P.

6
00:00:19,820 --> 00:00:23,812
CommonGround exposes twenty-seven typed browser tools.

7
00:00:23,812 --> 00:00:27,549
The agent does not scrape the page or guess where to click.

8
00:00:27,549 --> 00:00:35,458
It receives structured travelers, must-haves, preferences, budgets, hotel inventory, and the current scenario.

9
00:00:35,458 --> 00:00:41,567
It searches the normalized inventory and asks CommonGround to explain the group's actual trade-offs.

10
00:00:41,567 --> 00:00:49,718
The strongest conflict is clear: the beachfront favorite stretches the budget, while the accessible city option sacrifices the beach.

11
00:00:49,718 --> 00:00:53,889
With approval, the agent switches to Balanced Compromise.

12
00:00:53,889 --> 00:00:57,141
That is a real Web M C P write action.

13
00:00:57,141 --> 00:01:04,144
The visible interface changes immediately, the ranking is recalculated, and the action is logged for the group.

14
00:01:04,144 --> 00:01:12,626
Next, the agent prepares a booking draft with the selected hotel, dates, party size, price, and unresolved warnings.

15
00:01:12,626 --> 00:01:15,037
It cannot purchase anything.

16
00:01:15,037 --> 00:01:22,422
CommonGround deliberately stops at the human approval boundary, so automation is useful without becoming invisible or risky.

17
00:01:22,422 --> 00:01:27,014
This is also a complete group product, not a single demo screen.

18
00:01:27,014 --> 00:01:32,843
An organizer creates a private trip in three short steps, for up to thirty travelers.

19
00:01:32,843 --> 00:01:42,039
The guided checklist then helps them invite people by private link, choose predefined priorities, compare fair scenarios, and connect an agent.

20
00:01:42,039 --> 00:01:45,649
Each traveler controls only their own profile.

21
00:01:45,649 --> 00:01:55,241
Demo inventory can be replaced by TravelWithWadjet, Booking.com Demand, Expedia Rapid, or another licensed provider through one server-side adapter.

22
00:01:55,241 --> 00:02:02,116
Web M C P is the right fit because the agent and the humans share the same live state and the same visible interface.

23
00:02:02,116 --> 00:02:09,208
CommonGround turns a messy group chat into an explainable decision everyone can inspect, influence, and trust.

24
00:02:09,208 --> 00:02:15,623
CommonGround: group travel decisions that agents can help with, without taking control away from people.

